A||||8||ggarsk||It Died
Z||000000||ggarsk||08-22-99||04:56 PM||||While pulling into a parking spot my 84 4banger just died.....I have no juice going to anything. The battery has a full charge. Does anyone have a idea and/or suggestions of how to track down this problem. This is a great place to find info on Fieros. 
Z||000001||Stenny||08-22-99||05:20 PM||||My son's Fiero did that once. Turned out to be a corroded battery cable. There is also another wire that goes to ground right from the battery, this has caused some problems too. Good Luck!!
Z||000002||Dave85||08-22-99||10:20 PM||||It could be the ignition module. The lady that I bought my car from said it just died and wouldn't start. I bought a fully loaded '85 GT for $500. 2 minutes and $35 later I now have a great car. 
Z||000003||lowCG||08-22-99||11:12 PM||||OK, since the ogre hasn't said it yet,how about your fusible link(s) that go from the main power cables,back by the battery?<br>A test light will help greatly at times of major power outages.
Z||000004||ggarsk||08-23-99||01:31 AM||||I went to check out the fusible link...somebody has done a major rewiring of this car it it wasn't profeessional. I got small gauge wires sliced to large gauge. One fusible link is just some solid copper wire. I think I need to just get another wiring harness and start from scratch. I just bought this car for 300 and what little I've drove it I love it.Thanks for your replies.
Z||000005||theogre||08-23-99||07:44 AM||||check the small leads from the battery. those will kill it.<p>the terminal block is known for getting flaky. try pulling the connector heads off and reseating them. there is a bolt locking them down.
Z||000006||DJRice||08-23-99||07:57 AM||||As a matter of fact, I was in my 84 this weekend, and that little red wire that feeds everything to the car came loose.  Just like that, nothing.  <p>I vote that we rename that wire....It should now be called the 'SPF wire'.  SPF being Single Point Failure.....
Z||000007||ggarsk||08-24-99||02:38 AM||||It Runs!!! I got the wiring fixed,it was the fusible link or I should say lack of one that was the problem. It was fried. i cleaned up some of the wiring mess the last owner had donw too. Next is getting both my headlight to work. Thanks for all of your input!
Z||000008||theogre||08-24-99||09:57 AM||||I call it the microsoft or the blue screen wire. I think it's where Gate's and friends got the idea for the GPF.
